## Wire bfs_traversal to the adjacency + entity-search companions

Context: Task 8 of the cached graph reads plan — the highest-risk task.
`GraphDBBackend.bfs_traversal`, called (via `DigitalTwin.find_triples_bfs`)
by MCP's `describe_entity` tool and Graph Chat's find-and-traverse flow, now
seeds from `entity_search_seed_sql` (Task 4) and walks `_adj_out`/`_adj_in`
via `seeded_bfs_sql` (Task 5) when both companions are ready, falling back
to the existing `WITH RECURSIVE` SPO CTE (built from the caller-supplied
`seed_where`) when they are not, or on a missing-table error mid-query. The
seed-input threading was already resolved by earlier tasks: `bfs_traversal`
already accepted `search`/`entity_type` as separate optional parameters
(alongside `seed_where`), and `DigitalTwin.find_triples_bfs` already passed
them through — this task only had to consume them.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBBackend.py
   Import `seeded_bfs_sql` (adjacency) and `entity_search_seed_sql`
   (entity_search); prepend the companion-aware branch to `bfs_traversal`,
   leaving the legacy SPO recursive-CTE body unchanged as the fallback.
2. tests/units/graphdb/test_graphdb_adjacency_contract.py
   Add 4 FakeStore contract tests: companion path used when both ready,
   fallback when adjacency not ready, fallback when entity-search not
   ready, fallback on a missing-table error mid-query (2-call sequence).
3. tests/units/core/test_lakebase_flat_store.py
   Add `table_exists` mock to the existing `test_bfs_traversal_sql_path`
   (now required because `bfs_traversal` probes readiness before falling
   back — the unmocked call previously never touched `table_exists` and a
   live pool connection isn't available in this unit test) and add
   `test_bfs_traversal_uses_companions_when_ready` for the companion SQL.
4. tests/units/dtwin/test_digitaltwin_api.py
   `TestBfsTraversalSql._capture_sql` uses a bare
   `MagicMock(spec=GraphDBBackend)`; `adjacency_ready`/`entity_search_ready`
   now default to a truthy `MagicMock()` return value instead of `False`,
   which entered the new companion branch and blew up unpacking
   `adjacency_table_ids()`. Pin both to `False` so this class keeps testing
   only the legacy SPO SQL generation it was written for.

